{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery","id":961864,"title":"Mortars and artillery..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T13:26:15-07:00","id":961864,"title":"Mortars and artillery..","content":"Over on one of my Star wars D6 sites, we are having a discussion revolving around artillery and mortars, and the discussion got into whether pcs would stand a greater chance than the normal person to 'detect' incoming rounds of artillery/mortars before they got hit...<br /> For a werewolf/Vampire game where these were used, what would you say the difficulty would be, for say a Perception+alertness check to detect them enough to get a dodge?<br /> Would you need a gift or discipline active to get said check??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:06:28-07:00","id":961892,"title":"","content":"Well, it would not be possible to detect artillery with mortal senses if it is fired beyond the horizon because artillery is supersonic. Mortars are subsonic and close range (comparatively), so humans can detect them easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T21:52:47-07:00","id":962072,"title":"","content":"So for mortars, say one of the smaller calibers such as the UK's 40mm mortar, or the french LGI 50mm.. What would the diff be on a Per check to hear the shell being fired?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T21:58:52-07:00","id":962078,"title":"","content":"Vampires would need a celerity and auspex combo to see it, though you can roll unmodified auspex for the realisation that a bomb land next to you. Maybe blood magic could do it.<br /> Garou would need a gift.<br /> <br /> If you're doing a high level game, maybe soak. Garou can get rediculous soak at high levels, a powerful artillery round can do 30 dice of damage, and a garou's soak pool can exceed that. . vampires can fair OK with better fortitude, especially if you half bashing. Better fortitude rules might say that at some point, damage difficulties become +1 and at another soak difficulties become -1, with +2 -2 available at elder levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:01:05-07:00","id":962137,"title":"","content":"You will hear a mortal round as soon as it fires because it is subsonic. It is loud enough so that deaf people can hear lithe whistle in their bones. It is simple impossible to not notice the whistle unless there is a barrage. <br /> <br /> I think that an artillery round would probably do 1 dice of damage per millimeter of diameter (-10 per meter from the target for explosive rounds). Soak is really meaningless against that type of attack, at least for anything less durable than a main battle tank or a destroyer. Anyway, no vampire should ever have to worry about artillery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:17:16-07:00","id":962140,"title":"","content":"It's not like vampires can't get caught up in semi-active zones of military conflict (Israel during a rocket attack, Gaza during the inevitable Israeli retaliation, active political fault lines in the former Soviet states, etc.) or outright warzones, such that they might incidentally be exposed to artillery being deployed into or deliberately against civilian areas. I wouldn't put it completely past the Sabbat to get their hands on some mortars or something to facilitate an assault against a hard target during a Siege (I mean, it'll attract a lot of unwanted pressure from the authorities afterwards that could impede further Sabbat activity, but not everyone thinks these things through).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 09-02-2016, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:33:00-07:00","id":962267,"title":"","content":"I think mortars are much more survivable and more likely for a vampire to encounter than artillery. A vampire or werewolf that is hit by an artillery round should be considered to be a dead, as the standard US artillery is an M119 Howitzer, which launches a 14 kilogram projectile at 500 meters per second, giving it a kinetic energy of around 1,750,000 Joules (the average arrow possesses 75 Joules of kinetic energy by comparison). Nothing that takes 4 dice of damage from an arrow is going to have a chance of surviving a direct hit by artillery (superhuman senses may allow you to dodge it though, allowing a vampire or werewolf to have a chance of surviving). If you want though, let them try to soak around 120 dice of lethal damage, which is what I would consider to be a reasonable approximation of the damage from a direct hit of a M119 Howitzer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:20:57-07:00","id":962436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962137#post962137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will hear a mortal round as soon as it fires because it is subsonic. It is loud enough so that deaf people can hear lithe whistle in their bones. It is simple impossible to not notice the whistle unless there is a barrage.<br /> <br /> I think that an artillery round would probably do 1 dice of damage per millimeter of diameter (-10 per meter from the target for explosive rounds). Soak is really meaningless against that type of attack, at least for anything less durable than a main battle tank or a destroyer. Anyway, no vampire should ever have to worry about artillery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The damage given for heavy weapons in the V:tM 2nd edition player's guide and Rage Across the Amazon puts the damage far lower, with &quot;small mortars&quot; (total unit weight 50 lbs) at 12 dice and larger ones (unit weight 660 lbs) at 24 dice. 122mm howitzers, for reference, are 30 dice, and tank cannons are 20 to 30 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T13:52:18-07:00","id":962481,"title":"","content":"Yes, but that is because no one in White Wolf either understood ballistics or cared about ballistics. If you want to make something more consistent with reality, I would really suggest going with 1 dice of damage per millimeter of diameter. If you want neonate vampires to possibly survive direct hits from a 122mm howitzer (a Stamina 4 neonate with Fortitude 3 will take an average of 12 health levels of lethal damage from a direct hit with one success, which is halved to 6 health levels because it is a ballistic weapon), go ahead and use the default figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:35:22-07:00","id":962502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962137#post962137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will hear a mortal round as soon as it fires because it is subsonic. It is loud enough so that deaf people can hear lithe whistle in their bones. It is simple impossible to not notice the whistle unless there is a barrage.<br /> <br /> I think that an artillery round would probably do 1 dice of damage per millimeter of diameter (-10 per meter from the target for explosive rounds). Soak is really meaningless against that type of attack, at least for anything less durable than a main battle tank or a destroyer. Anyway, no vampire should ever have to worry about artillery.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO that depends on how close you are. A 65mm mortar at say 600 yards away, can hit you , but i doubt you would hear the 'thomp'.. Maybe at 200m you might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962140#post962140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like vampires can't get caught up in semi-active zones of military conflict (Israel during a rocket attack, Gaza during the inevitable Israeli retaliation, active political fault lines in the former Soviet states, etc.) or outright warzones, such that they might incidentally be exposed to artillery being deployed into or deliberately against civilian areas. I wouldn't put it completely past the Sabbat to get their hands on some mortars or something to facilitate an assault against a hard target during a Siege (I mean, it'll attract a lot of unwanted pressure from the authorities afterwards that could impede further Sabbat activity, but not everyone thinks these things through).</div> </div> </div> </div>Addionally, Garou often get involved in conflicts with Pentex and such which could have mortar or artillery defenses..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:47:59-07:00","id":962510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962481#post962481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that is because no one in White Wolf either understood ballistics or cared about ballistics. If you want to make something more consistent with reality, I would really suggest going with 1 dice of damage per millimeter of diameter. If you want neonate vampires to possibly survive direct hits from a 122mm howitzer (a Stamina 4 neonate with Fortitude 3 will take an average of 12 health levels of lethal damage from a direct hit with one success, which is halved to 6 health levels because it is a ballistic weapon), go ahead and use the default figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artillery damage typically isn't from ballistics as in raw KE damage, but from the payload; it's the difference between being shot at and having a bomb detonated around you. Also, it's not reasonable to allow vampires to halve the damage of explosives and big guns, because those weapons aren't killing people because they're hitting vital organs or the like, but because support weapons and vehicular-mounted guns are so utterly destructive that they typically turn soft targets to hamburger or pink mist. Vampires would also tend to get turned into hamburger and pink mist alongside mortals, and should take full damage accordingly.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's true that WW was, and in many cases still is bad with math, but vampires should be getting splatted alongside normal humans unless they have plot device Fortitude. Also, the ST can always rule that, because the damage and breeching rules were on a different scale, that hamburger and pink mist automatically result from use of these weapons on a soft target, no roll necessary unless you have an outrageously high soak pool or somehow are closer to or even beyond the scale of the weapon extremely large Mokole might treat tank cannons as rifles or pistols, for example, and layered soak Gifts in Crinos might allow Garou and Fera to survive being in the effect zone (good thing no one can really justify an industrialized process for making silver artillery rounds, and gold flak is right out). There's also some indication that whatever scale of increase gets used for dice pools might not work with a strict bore size to dice system. The V Revised ST booklet with the screen suggests that approach, I think. For those who do get a roll, however, you'd probably be better served by re-scaling things to make them manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:49:28-07:00","id":962513,"title":"","content":"I do not know, I can hear a 30-06 from 2 or 3 miles away because it is around 160 decibels. An M224 mortar is around 180 decibels (<a href=\"http://www.vi.ngb.army.mil/html/safety/docs/Noise%20in%20Army%20Equipment.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.vi.ngb.army.mil/html/safe...0Equipment.pdf</a>), so I imagine you could hear it from 8 to 12 miles away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:51:19-07:00","id":962514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962502#post962502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Addionally, Garou often get involved in conflicts with Pentex and such which could have mortar or artillery defenses..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Significantly less often now, since the Amazon pullout by just about all parties. Pentex doesn't make much money firing its own artillery into a jungle, so they wouldn't have kept that up for very long. They make out better when someone else pays them for those shells instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:54:17-07:00","id":962516,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Pentex is better off corrupting humans for fun and profit, since corrupted humans will go off an destroy the environment on their own initiative without Pentex needing to lift a finger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:26:42-07:00","id":962528,"title":"","content":"I usually just handle Artillery (the one time it came up) as doing levels of damage instead of dice. It takes out a lot of the randomized factor in whether or not something can survive it. And damage, especially on the high end is more and more of an abstraction. 30 levels of damage does pretty much auto-kill anything outside of the truly monstrous enemies in the WoD, which works just fine.<br /> <br /> There is the possibility of a soak specialized Garou or Vampire that is prepared for such an attack to survive, but at that point you are planning damage around an individual as opposed to the system.<br /> <br /> Per dodging, I would allow dodging for mortars assuming the being in question has reasonable knowledge of the attack. They really do area damage anyway, so maybe just have the dodge grant soak dice against the damage. Dodging Artillery is a weird concept, but certainly some beings in the WoD can do it. I seem to remember dodging a bullet without cover being Dif 9, so maybe allow the same roll if the creature is aware of the attack. Possibly count every 2 successes as 1 if you really want to penalize the dodge attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-02-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:47:41-07:00","id":962566,"title":"","content":"Well, you are dodging the probably path of the bullet rather than the bullet if you are aware of it. I think that I would require superhuman senses to dodge artillery, since it would be otherwise impossible to get behind cover because you are otherwise unaware of the threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:32:06-07:00","id":962621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962566#post962566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you are dodging the probably path of the bullet rather than the bullet if you are aware of it. I think that I would require superhuman senses to dodge artillery, since it would be otherwise impossible to get behind cover because you are otherwise unaware of the threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's less important than the fact that when the shell hits, it doesn't just hit a point, it explodes over an area. Can you instantly jump dozens of meters in the time it takes to get out of the way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:27:39-07:00","id":962663,"title":"","content":"Yeah, your only hope is to detect it at the height of its progress. You could get travel fifteen meters in three seconds. Of course, if you have Celerity or Rage, you might be able to run forty-five meters in that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:41:05-07:00","id":962668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/961864-mortars-and-artillery?p=962663#post962663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, your only hope is to detect it at the height of its progress. You could get travel fifteen meters in three seconds. Of course, if you have Celerity or Rage, you might be able to run forty-five meters in that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or for Garou, 